<!-- ClickHouse's MergeTree rules kept as 26.2 has them, where 26.8 changed
     them (workplan 0119 §3 item 9, option 2, the owner's decision of
     2026-11-02: 26.8.36.3-lts, ahead of the 26.2.19.43 Trigger.dev v4.8.3
     pins). Read at v26.8.34.13-lts, the newest public 26.8 tag; 26.8.36.3,
     a security release, has none.

     allow_dimensions_outside_sorting_key = 1. From 26.7 the default is
     false (src/Core/SettingsChangesHistory.cpp, the 26.7 MergeTree block),
     and an AggregatingMergeTree is refused at CREATE, BAD_ARGUMENTS, when a
     column is neither in its ORDER BY or PARTITION BY nor an aggregate state
     (src/Storages/MergeTree/MergeTreeData.cpp: the check runs when
     `mode <= CREATE`, so a table already on a volume is attached unchecked).
     Trigger.dev's migration 022 (internal-packages/clickhouse/schema/
     022_create_errors_v1_table.sql at v4.8.3) has three: error_type,
     error_message and sample_stack_trace. On an empty volume goose stops
     there, and trigger-api, whose entrypoint runs it under `set -e`,
     crash-loops: a new install, a new host, a reset. 1 is 26.2's rule.

     auto_statistics_types = '' (empty). From 26.4 the default writes column
     statistics into every new part ('basic, uniq_v2' at 26.8; '' at 26.2 and
     26.3), applied when a table loads as well as when it is created
     (src/Storages/MergeTree/registerStorageMergeTree.cpp). 26.2 and 26.3 read
     only the oldest statistics format, and Trigger.dev v4.8.3 has never run
     with them. Empty writes none (addImplicitStatistics returns at once on
     '', src/Storages/Statistics/Statistics.cpp).

     How it reaches every table: Context::getMergeTreeSettings applies
     `compatibility`, then this <merge_tree> section
     (src/Interpreters/Context.cpp), and every MergeTree table's settings
     start from those (registerStorageMergeTree.cpp).

     IT TRAVELS WITH THE PIN. A 26.2 or 26.3 server does not start with it
     mounted: allow_dimensions_outside_sorting_key is unknown there, and an
     unknown key under <merge_tree> stops the server (UNKNOWN_SETTING, read at
     v26.3.60.2-lts). A checkout that pins an older ClickHouse mounts neither
     this file nor clickhouse-users-profile.xml.

     A file of its own rather than a line in clickhouse-override.xml, which is
     upstream's tuning verbatim and says so. docs/managed-bring-up.md, "Moving
     ClickHouse", has the check that both values are in force. -->
<clickhouse>
    <merge_tree>
        <allow_dimensions_outside_sorting_key>1</allow_dimensions_outside_sorting_key>
        <auto_statistics_types></auto_statistics_types>
    </merge_tree>
</clickhouse>
